    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to start by determining how many days week in total there are (from Monday to Sunday) in November. Since there are 11 days (Nov 1 → Nov 11) in November, the day of the week of the 11th changes by 1 (Monday to Tuesday, Tuesday to Wednesday, and so on). Then, we need to see how many more days pass from the 23rd of November to the 23rd of December. For that, we need to know the day of the week for November 23, which we already know is a Thursday.\n\nThus, the number of days between November 23 and December 23 equals 30 days (November 23 → November 30 → December 23). Since the 23rd of November was a Thursday, adding 30 days yields a Saturday.\n\nNow, the 30th is on Friday if the day of the week before the 23rd was a Thursday, which is next to the last Thursday. Thus, the 30th, which corresponds to ongoing on December 23, falls on a Friday.",
