    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's use a Friday as the base day: 5 Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, Monday, Tuesday {begin\\_day:3, end\\_day:5} {begin\\_month:11, end\\_month:12}  {begin\\_day:6} {1}\n\n1. When November 23 falls on Thursday, a one-day offset rotates the remaining days 4 weeks up, since 90 falls between the 4 full weeks and November 23. Therefore, December 23 falls on {begin\\_day:1} {month:12, end\\_day:23} {end\\_month:11} {div\\_12} {end\\_day:2}, or Monday.",
