    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the day of the week that December 23 falls on if Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to count the number of days between the two dates and then use modular arithmetic to find the day that corresponds to that number of days.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the difference between November 23 and December 23.\nFrom November 23 to December 1 is 9 days long. November has 30 days, so from November 1 to November 23 is 23 days long. Thus, the total days from November 1 to December 23 is:\n\\[\n30 \\text{ days} + 9 \\text{ days} = 39 \\text{ days}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Simplify the problem by finding days of the week.\nAdding 39 days to any day of the week will result in one day of the week ahead. We start at Thursday (let's denote this as \\(A\\)). Adding 9 days to \\(A\\) (which is 1 more day) on a 7-day cycle adds \\(1\\) day. Therefore, adding 39 days is equivalent to adding \\(1\\) day \\(39 - 36 = 3\\) times as well as adding those extra remaining \\(3\\) days to the same \\(A\\).\n\\[\n(1 \\times 1) + 3 \\times 1 = A + 4 \\equiv A + 4 \\equiv A + 4 \\equiv A + 4-7 \\equiv A + 7 \\equiv A \\in \\text{Sunday}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Conclusion.\nDecember 23 falls accordingly on Sunday.\n\nThus, the solution to the problem is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\n\\]",
